The committed budgets are contract inputs, not measurements from a developer
workstation.  `ledger-full.txt` and `ledger-minimal.txt` must be generated only
by the pinned x86_64-linux-gnu CI measurement described by Sprint 57.  They are
intentionally absent until that lane is wired and produces provenance-bearing
output.

The four single-module values are the Sprint 57 contract caps.  When the first
pinned ledgers land, their `why` fields must be replaced with the measured
minimal-plus-module derivation and rounded upward to the next 10 KiB; a local
developer build is not acceptable provenance for that update.
